---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site, href } from "../data/site";
import modelCsv from "../data/cost/cost_model.csv?raw";
import summary from "../data/cost/cost_summary.json";
import check from "../data/cost/cost_check.json";

// What a rebuild would cost, from the realistic scenario of the cost model (src/data/cost/, counted
// at the release tags on 2026-10-22), all 19 packages including janusplot.
function parseCsv(text: string): Record<string, string>[] {
  const rows: string[][] = [];
  let row: string[] = [], cell = "", q = false;
  for (let i = 0; i < text.length; i++) {
    const c = text[i];
    if (q) { if (c === '"' && text[i + 1] === '"') { cell += '"'; i++; } else if (c === '"') q = false; else cell += c; }
    else if (c === '"') q = true;
    else if (c === ",") { row.push(cell); cell = ""; }
    else if (c === "\n") { row.push(cell); rows.push(row); row = []; cell = ""; }
    else if (c !== "\r") cell += c;
  }
  if (cell || row.length) { row.push(cell); rows.push(row); }
  const [head, ...body] = rows;
  return body.filter((r) => r.length === head.length).map((r) => Object.fromEntries(head.map((h, i) => [h, r[i]])));
}
const rows = parseCsv(modelCsv).filter((r) => r.scenario === "realistic");
const tot = (pred: (r: Record<string, string>) => boolean, f: "cost_aud" | "hours") =>
  rows.filter(pred).reduce((s, r) => s + Number(r[f]), 0);
const groups = [
  ["package", "R packages (19)", "Effort from each package's size in logical statements at its release, by COCOMO II, with testing and documentation"],
  ["contract", "Shared result format", "Effort from its size, as for the packages"],
  ["data", "DataHub", "Enrolling and measuring the datasets it holds"],
  ["study", "Studies", "Hours per study, from the studies on record"],
  ["publication", "Website, poster and papers", "Hours per page, poster and paper"],
  ["governance", "Decision records and audits", "Hours per record and per audit"],
  ["overhead", "Coordination", "A share of the team hours above"],
] as const;
const table = groups.map(([g, label, basis]) =>
  ({ label, basis, hours: tot((r) => r.group === g, "hours"), cost: tot((r) => r.group === g, "cost_aud") }));
const total = { hours: table.reduce((s, r) => s + r.hours, 0), cost: table.reduce((s, r) => s + r.cost, 0) };
const ratio = total.cost / summary.scenarios.realistic.total_aud;
const band = { low: summary.scenarios.realistic.band_aud.low * ratio, high: summary.scenarios.realistic.band_aud.high * ratio };
const years = total.hours / check.hours_per_year;
const checks = check.checks.map((c) => ({ ...c, cost: years * c.salary_aud * (1 + check.on_cost) }));
const aud = (x: number, to = 1000) => `$${(Math.round(x / to) * to).toLocaleString("en-AU")}`;
const audM = (x: number) => `$${(x / 1e6).toFixed(2)} million`;
const n0 = (x: number) => Math.round(x).toLocaleString("en-AU");
---
<Base title="About" description="Why the orchestra is built the way it is, which data it uses, and how its results are recorded." path="/about">
  <section class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="kicker">About</p>
      <h1>R packages for crop decisions based on cause and effect</h1>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="lead">A model that fits an outcome well can still rest on an association nobody
        has checked. A pipeline that tunes a model and then optimises against it will act on that
        association. The orchestra is built so that it does not.</p>

      <h2 class="mt-3">Two rules</h2>
      <p class="mt-1"><strong>Withhold when unsure.</strong> A package gives no result when the
        evidence is too thin, when independent methods disagree, or when an input has not been
        checked. It records why, and the decision packages do not price a withheld answer.</p>
      <p class="mt-2"><strong>Check against an outside reference.</strong> Every fact about an
        outside source, such as a dataset's columns, a constant or a citation, is checked against
        a reference the orchestra did not produce. Unchecked facts are not used.</p>

      <h2 class="mt-3">Where every result came from</h2>
      <p class="mt-1">Each result is saved in the shared record every package writes. It names the
        package and version that produced it, the earlier records it was built from, and a
        checksum that fails if anything is altered, so every number in a report can be traced
        back to the record it came from.</p>

      <h2 class="mt-3">Data</h2>
      <p class="mt-1">{site.domain}. The sowing-time study uses open data: the trial records compiled by
        Newman and Furbank (2021) and published under CC BY 4.0, analysed as they are, with ABARES statistics
        for the wheat price. The nitrogen study concerns the GRDC Barley Synthesis trials, which are
        confidential: its page shows only numbers from a synthetic copy, made by {"{masque}"} with a known
        answer planted in it, and the real rows stay with their holder. Package tests also use simulated data
        built around a known answer. No GRDC-origin code or data enters any package.</p>

      <h2 class="mt-3">Licence</h2>
      <p class="mt-1">The public packages are released under the MIT licence through{" "}
        <code>max578.r-universe.dev</code>. The others are still in development.</p>

      <h2 class="mt-3" id="cost">What it would cost to build</h2>
      <p class="mt-1">Built again from scratch by a small senior team, the 19 packages, DataHub, the studies and the
        records behind them would cost about <strong>{audM(total.cost)}</strong>, or {n0(total.hours)} hours,
        about {years.toFixed(1)} person-years.</p>
    </div>
    <section class="table-scroll mt-2" tabindex="0" aria-label="Cost of building the orchestra, by item"><table class="num t-wide">
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Item</th><th scope="col">Basis</th><th scope="col">Hours</th><th scope="col">A$</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {table.map((r) => <tr><th scope="row">{r.label}</th><td>{r.basis}</td><td>{n0(r.hours)}</td><td>{aud(r.cost)}</td></tr>)}
      </tbody>
      <tfoot><tr><th scope="row">Total</th><td></td><td>{n0(total.hours)}</td><td>{aud(total.cost)}</td></tr></tfoot>
    </table></section>
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="mt-2"><strong>Method.</strong> Hours are priced at Australian pay rates for each role (university,
        CSIRO and industry scales, with on-costs). The team is three senior data scientists, with part-time help from a
        professor-level methodologist, a research software lead and a crop scientist. Plausible settings of the method
        give {audM(band.low)} to {audM(band.high)}.</p>
      <p class="mt-2"><strong>Independent check.</strong> The same {years.toFixed(1)} person-years, at {n0(check.hours_per_year)} working
        hours a year and {Math.round(100 * check.on_cost)}% on-costs, priced on published pay rates read on 25 October 2026:</p>
      <ul class="mt-1">
        {checks.map((c) => <li>{c.label}: {audM(c.cost)} (<a href={c.url}>{c.source}</a>)</li>)}
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-2">The estimate sits at the top of the university range, as expected for a senior team, and well above
        the national average wage.</p>

      <h2 class="mt-3">Acknowledgement</h2>
      <p class="mt-1">{site.acknowledgement}</p>

      <p class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={href("/members")}>The members</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={href("/examples")}>The studies</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
